 "notes": [
  {
   "kind": "review",
   "text": "Increasing/decreasing test (p.99) has two misprints: the clause \"f(x₁) ≥ f(x₂)\" should be \"f is continuous on I\", and c, d say \"f′(x) > 0 and f′(x) = 0\", which should be \"f′(x) > 0 (zero only at isolated points)\". Lessons use the corrected test."
  },
  {
   "kind": "note",
   "text": "Example 2 writes \"increasing on [−1, 0] ∪ [2, ∞)\". It increases on each interval separately, not on the union (f(0) = 5 > f(1) = −8); lessons say \"on [−1, 0] and [2, ∞)\"."
  }
 ],
